            <div xml:id="d842">

                <pb facs="0794" n="694" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg694"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">311.6124/16: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commissioner at Helsingfors</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Haynes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Helsingfors</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-09T20:00:00+01:39"><hi rendition="#italic">January 9,
                                1920—8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 10—3
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>518. Department’s telegram of January 7, 6 p.m. Have succeeded gaining consent
                    and cooperation in every way for transfer through Hangö. Attacks against Finnish
                    Government sure to result, but to no probable permanent effect. Awaiting
                    definite decision as to Hangö.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Haynes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
